.TH SDL_getenv_unsafe 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_getenv_unsafe \- Get the value of a variable in the environment.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_getenv_unsafe(const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function bypasses SDL\(aqs cached copy of the environment and is not thread-safe\[char46]
.PP
On some platforms, this may make case-insensitive matches, while other platforms are case-sensitive\[char46] It is best to be precise with strings used for queries through this interface\[char46]
.BR SDL_getenv
is always case-sensitive, however\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I name
the name of the variable to get\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the value of the variable or NULL if it can\(aqt be found\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function is not thread safe, consider using
.BR SDL_getenv ()
instead\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

